    "pathway_role_summary": "TCF7L2 is a critical effector of canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling. In the absence of Wnt signal, TCF7L2 recruits Groucho/TLE corepressors to inhibit target gene transcription. Upon Wnt stimulation, beta-catenin accumulates in the nucleus, displaces corepressors from TCF7L2, and converts it into a transcriptional activator. The beta-catenin/TCF7L2 complex regulates expression of genes involved in cell proliferation (MYC, CCND1), stem cell maintenance (LGR5), and glucose homeostasis. TCF7L2 plays essential roles in intestinal epithelial stem cell maintenance, pancreatic beta-cell function, liver metabolism, and adipocyte differentiation. Dysregulation contributes to colorectal cancer (80-90% have APC/CTNNB1 mutations affecting Wnt pathway) and type 2 diabetes."
  },
  "disease_associations": [
    {
      "disease": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus",
      "omim_id": "125853",
      "mutation_type": "Germline polymorphisms (SNPs)",
      "description": "TCF7L2 is the T2D-associated gene with the largest effect on disease susceptibility. SNP rs7903146 (C>T) shows OR=1.87 for TT vs CC genotype. SNPs rs12255372 and rs290481 also significantly associated. Polymorphisms affect glucose homeostasis, insulin secretion, and pancreatic beta-cell function."
    },
    {
      "disease": "Colorectal cancer",
      "omim_id": "114500",
      "mutation_type": "Somatic mutations / altered expression",
      "description": "TCF7L2 belongs to most frequently mutated genes in CRC. Paradoxical tumor suppressor role - loss of nuclear TCF7L2 promotes migration and invasion. 80-90% of CRC contain mutations in APC or CTNNB1 affecting Wnt pathway. TCF7L2 directly suppresses pro-metastatic RUNX2 and impacts cell adhesion molecules."
    },
    {
      "disease": "Hepatocellular carcinoma",
      "omim_id": "114550",
      "mutation_type": "Altered expression",
      "description": "TCF7L2 promotes metastasis via NEDD9-mediated activation of AKT/mTOR signaling pathway. Spatial transcriptional activity of hepatic TCF7L2 regulates zonated metabolic pathways contributing to liver fibrosis."
    },
    {
